{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-c68ebed3-b396-47b2-8c82-b5715451e741","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a9af91e7bb9ca7c1","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-y1gfxeze/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8010-E002.md","content":"# Cloudmanager binary reconciliation log standardization with structured resource context\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic applies the same structured logging convention to the rhods-operator\n**cloudmanager** binary, which handles multi-cloud infrastructure dependencies on\nnon-OpenShift Kubernetes (AWS EKS, Azure AKS, CoreWeave). Its reconciliation controllers\n(AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine, CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine) are built on the\nsame controller-runtime/logr foundation using the shared reconciler pattern, so they\nalready receive `name` and `namespace` from controller-runtime's request logger. The\nremaining work is converting message-embedded resource identity in error paths to\nstructured key-value pairs, adding `resourceKind` (the kind is not implied by these\ncontrollers' names), migrating any non-standard key names if present, and wiring the\nmirror CI lint check for the cloudmanager binary's surfaces. This epic is independently\nschedulable from the manager-binary work and may land in the same or a subsequent release\nat PM discretion.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Audit all `log.Error()` call sites in reconciliation error paths across the three\n  cloudmanager controllers (AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine,\n  CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine).\n- For every call site embedding resource name or namespace in the message string, extract\n  the identity fields and convert to structured KV pairs (`name`, `namespace`).\n- Add `resourceKind` as a structured field to all cloudmanager reconciliation error logs.\n- Migrate any non-standard structured key names to the camelCase convention\n  (`name`/`namespace`/`resourceKind`), mirroring the DSCI migration if non-standard keys\n  are found during the audit.\n- Add unit tests that parse test logger output and assert `name`, `namespace`, and\n  `resourceKind` presence and correctness for the cloudmanager controllers.\n- Add a CI lint / static-analysis check that flags any `log.Error` call in the\n  cloudmanager binary's controllers that embeds name/namespace in the message text or is\n  missing the required structured fields, wired into CI for the cloudmanager binary's\n  surfaces (this epic owns the enforcement for exactly the surfaces it converts).\n- Backwards-compatibility validation per the strategy NFR: before/after log output\n  comparison for a sample reconciliation error, with the production log consumers\n  relevant to cloudmanager deployments (e.g., CloudWatch) verified to ingest both formats\n  without configuration changes.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a cloudmanager controller (AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine,\n  CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine) encounters a reconciliation error, the log entry includes\n  `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` as structured fields — measured by a unit test\n  asserting field presence and correctness in test logger output.\n- No cloudmanager reconciliation error log call embeds resource name or namespace in the\n  message string — measured by the CI lint rule / static analysis flagging zero remaining\n  violations across the cloudmanager binary's controllers.\n- Before/after log output comparison for a sample cloudmanager reconciliation error\n  confirms the structured fields appear and the sample log consumer ingests both formats\n  without configuration changes.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): all rhods-operator reconciliation error logs embedding resource name or\n  namespace in message strings are converted to structured KV pairs (`name`,\n  `namespace`) — cloudmanager-binary portion.\n- HLR-5 (P0): all cloudmanager controller (AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine,\n  CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine) reconciliation error logs include `name`, `namespace`, and\n  `resourceKind` as structured fields.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":63957,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bdbe1c6b5d9e58e8","agent_id":"a1e7319239208d111","session_id":"63a747e2-9d8d-4636-a22b-5d195afcf157","uuid":"1e9e6ccd-a39b-43ac-90bf-740765d83aff","timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:40:57.316Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8010 into epics"}
