{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bd537db48fa27ae8","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8010-E003\n3\ttitle: Structured log field convention documentation and external publication\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8010\n5\tcomponent: OpenShift AI Productization\n6\tteam: ODH Operator team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\timplementation_type: docs-authoring\n10\tdependencies:\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8010-E001\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8010-E002\n13\tai_signals:\n14\t  change_specificity: 1\n15\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n16\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n17\t  existing_foundation: 1\n18\t  open_questions: -1\n19\t  external_dependency: 0\n20\t  human_process_gates: -1\n21\t  repo_access: 1\n22\t  architecture_claims: 1\n23\tinvestigation_signals: null\n24\tai_implementability: Medium\n25\tai_implementability_score: 2\n26\tjira_key: null\n27\tbranch: null\n28\tgated_by: null\n29\tgate_failure_impact: null\n30\t---\n31\t# Structured log field convention documentation and external publication\n32\t\n33\t## Description\n34\t\n35\tThis epic authors and publishes the documentation deliverable of the strategy: a\n36\tcontribution guideline specifying the structured log field convention for rhods-operator\n37\tcontrollers (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`, camelCase naming), explaining the\n38\tthree-problem diagnosis that motivated it, and providing before/after code examples drawn\n39\tfrom the completed conversion work in both rhods-operator binaries. It also publishes the\n40\tconvention for voluntary adoption by external operator teams (Cluster Observability\n41\tOperator: Loki Operator, Tempo Operator) per platform policy (overlay 0008 — RHOAI does\n42\tnot install, manage, or control external operator dependencies), and documents the DSCI\n43\tkey-name migration for operators with existing log queries. This is substantive content\n44\tauthoring, distinct from the code conversion, and follows the Red Hat docs content\n45\tprocess.\n46\t\n47\t## Scope\n48\t\n49\tContent outline:\n50\t\n51\t- The structured log field convention: required fields (`name`, `namespace`,\n52\t  `resourceKind`), the camelCase naming rationale (alignment with controller-runtime's\n53\t  existing structured log key conventions), and guidance for cluster-scoped resources\n54\t  (namespace omitted or empty).\n55\t- The three-problem diagnosis: message-embedded identity, non-standard DSCI keys, and\n56\t  missing `resourceKind`.\n57\t- Before/after code examples for converting message-embedded resource identity to\n58\t  structured KV pairs, taken from the converted manager and cloudmanager controller code.\n59\t- A DSCI key-name migration guide (`Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization` →\n60\t  `name`/`namespace`) with before/after Loki/CloudWatch query examples, documented for\n61\t  release notes so the transition happens in a single release.\n62\t- The convention as a contribution guideline for new controller development in\n63\t  rhods-operator (what a new controller's error logs must emit and how the CI lint check\n64\t  enforces it).\n65\t- Publication of the convention for external operator adoption (Loki Operator, Tempo\n66\t  Operator) as a specification for voluntary adoption, plus tracking issues filed in the\n67\t  COO projects.\n68\t\n69\t## Acceptance Criteria\n70\t\n71\t- The contribution guideline specifies the required fields (`name`, `namespace`,\n72\t  `resourceKind`), the camelCase naming rationale, and the three-problem diagnosis\n73\t  (message-embedded identity, non-standard DSCI keys, missing `resourceKind`) — measured\n74\t  by review against the strategy's documentation acceptance criterion.\n75\t- The DSCI key migration is documented with before/after query examples suitable for\n76\t  release notes — measured by the migration guide covering both old and new field names.\n77\t- The guideline is technically reviewed against the implementation: a reviewer confirms\n78\t  the before/after examples match the converted log calls actually shipped in the\n79\t  rhods-operator manager and cloudmanager binaries.\n80\t- The convention is published in a form external operator teams (COO: Loki Operator,\n81\t  Tempo Operator) can adopt, and tracking issues are filed in the COO projects — measured\n82\t  by the published specification and the filed issues referencing it.\n83\t\n84\t## HLR Traceability\n85\t\n86\t- HLR-8 (P1): document the convention as a contribution guideline for new controller\n87\t  development and publish for external operator adoption.\n88\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a07fbabd4b7a6279","agent_id":"a2d85af158f7c4f33","session_id":"63a747e2-9d8d-4636-a22b-5d195afcf157","uuid":"15f65e76-d7ad-4230-a33e-ae90337bacc6","timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:46:54.005Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bd537db48fa27ae8","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review revised decomposition"}
