pstream contribution or vendor coordination is needed — controller-runtime's logr interface already supports arbitrary structured key-value pairs (internal dependency, status: exists). |\n14\t| human_process_gates | 0 | The epic's deliverable path (code, tests, lint wiring) needs no human approval step. SRE/Support coordination on text-based alert rules is informational coordination during validation, not an approval gate on the deliverable. |\n15\t| repo_access | +1 | The code is accessible: the architecture context documents both the downstream repo (red-hat-data-services/rhods-operator) and its public auto-merged upstream (opendatahub-io/opendatahub-operator), so the surfaces can be cloned and modified. |\n16\t| architecture_claims | +1 | The epic's scope is corroborated by `.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/rhods-operator.md`: it confirms the controller-runtime/logr foundation (go-logr/logr and sigs.k8s.io/controller-runtime dependencies), the DataScienceCluster/DSCInitialization CRDs and DSCInitializationReconciler, the component/service handler integration points, and the 8 component CRDs matching the named component controllers. (The context file summarizes the tiering more coarsely than the SME's 5-tier breakdown, but it does not contradict the surfaces in scope.) |\n17\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a07fbabd4b7a6279","agent_id":"a2d85af158f7c4f33","session_id":"63a747e2-9d8d-4636-a22b-5d195afcf157","uuid":"55af57f8-1963-4770-a02d-5af11d03157e","timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:46:57.613Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b6efe9bb1e9d445c","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review revised decomposition"}
